{"name":"Cauliflower Cream","hex":"#f2e4c7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cauliflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brassica oleracea var. botrytis, an annual variety of cabbage, of which the cluster of young flower stalks and buds is eaten as a vegetable.","The edible head or curd of a cauliflower plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To (cause to) swell up like a cauliflower ear."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cauliflower"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cauliflower","blocks":[{"text":"Cauliflower is a vegetable belonging to the species Brassica oleracea in the family Brassicaceae. It is one of several cultivated forms of the species along with cabbage, broccoli, Brussels sprouts, kale, kohlrabi, and others. The edible portion of the plant is its dense head of undeveloped flower buds known as the \"curd\". The head is usually white but may also be green, orange, or purple. Several cultivars exist, including the Romanesco variety, whose spiral curds grow in fractal patterns."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Chou-fleur_02.jpg/330px-Chou-fleur_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cauliflower"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg/500px-Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg/500px-Cauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cauliflower plants growing in a nursery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACauliflower_plants_growing_in_New_Jersey_in_April.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/Cauliflower_broccoflower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai